===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|scifi}} A person who works or lives in [[space]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1954|author=Isaac Asimov|title=The Caves of Steel|passage=It was the futile throwing back in the face of the '''Spacers''' their most keenly felt insult: their insistence on considering the natives of Earth as disgustingly diseased.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|origyear=1993|year=2014|author=Bruce Coville|title=Aliens Ate My Homework|passage="How do I know I can trust you?" asked BKR.<br />Grakker hesitated. "'''Spacer's''' oath," he said at last.|page=134|url=https://www.google.com/books/edition/Aliens_Ate_My_Homework/hYiEAAAAQBAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&dq=%22spacer%27s+oath%22&pg=PA134&printsec=frontcover}}
#* {{quote-video game|en|developer=w:BioWare|title={{w|Mass Effect (video game)|Mass Effect}}|location=Redwood City|publisher=Electronic Arts|year=2008|genre=[[science fiction|Science Fiction]]|system=PC|scene={{w|Citadel (Mass Effect)|Citadel}}|isbn=9780784546642|oclc=246633669|passage=Shepard: What are you running for?<br>Charles Saracino: I'm seeking one of the five '''spacer''' seats in Parliament. They have certain baroque conditions for a citizen to be able to vote for them.<br>Charles Saracino: You have to spend more than six months a year in space. But you can't have stayed in any one settled system for more than a month.}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=2017|author=A.K. Brown|title=Humans on the Menu|series=Champagne Universe Series: Book 2|page=20|passage=He was thankful that he still had his suit on when the ship had a catastrophic decompression, a '''spacer's''' worst nightmare.}}
# An object inserted to hold a [[space]] open in a row of items, e.g. [[bead]]s or printed [[type]].
# A [[bushing]].
# {{lb|en|slang}} A forgetful person; one who [[space out|spaces out]].
# {{lb|en|medicine}} A type of add-on device used by an [[asthmatic]] person to increase the effectiveness of a [[metered-dose inhaler]].
# {{lb|en|historical}} An [[instrument]] for [[reverse|reversing]] a [[telegraphic]] [[current]], especially in a marine cable, to increase the speed of transmission.

